solution:
Use the definition of factorial to simplify the expression:
   \begin{align*}
   \frac{9! \cdot 5! \cdot 2!}{8! \cdot 6!} &= \frac{(9 \cdot 8!) \cdot (5! \cdot 2!)}{(8!) \cdot (6 \cdot 5!)} \\
   &= \frac{(9 \cdot \cancel{8!}) \cdot (1 \cdot \cancel{5!} \cdot 2!)}{(\cancel{8!}) \cdot (6 \cdot \cancel{5!})} \\
   &= \frac{(9) \cdot (2!)}{(6)} \\
   &= \frac{(9) \cdot (2 \cdot 1!)}{(6)} \\
   &= \frac{(9) \cdot (2 \cdot 1)}{(6)} \\
   &= \boxed{3}
   \end{align*}

