   \begin{align*}
   16^3\times8^3&=(2^4)^3\times(2^3)^3\\
   &=(2^{4\times3})\times(2^{3\times3})\\
   &=2^{12}\times2^{9}
   \end{align*}

When we multiply two numbers with the same base together, we add the exponents:
\[ 2^{12}\times2^{9}=2^{12+9}=2^{21} \]

This expression is equal to $2^K$, so we can write
   \begin{align*}
