solution:
First rewrite $16^{7/4}$ as $(2^4)^{7/4}$, then simplify using exponent rules:
\begin{align*}
(2^4)^{7/4} &= 2^{4 \cdot 7/4} \Rightarrow 2^{(4 \cdot 7)/4} \Rightarrow 2^{28/4} \\
&\Rightarrow 2^7 \Rightarrow 2^7 = 128 \Rightarrow \boxed{128}
\end{align*}

