solution:
The given inequalities are
\begin{align*}
   \frac{1}{3} < \frac{x}{5} < \frac{5}{8}
\end{align*}
Multiply all inequalities by 120 to eliminate the fractions.
\[ 120 \cdot \frac{1}{3} < 120 \cdot \frac{x}{5} < 120 \cdot \frac{5}{8} \Rightarrow 40 < 24x < 75 \Rightarrow 40 \cdot \frac{1}{24} < x < 75 \cdot \frac{1}{24} \Rightarrow 1\frac{2}{3} < x < 3\frac{1}{8} \]
Thus, the largest integral value of $x$ satisfying the given inequalities is
\begin{align*}
   \boxed{3}
\end{align*}

