solution:
To find the result, subtract the corresponding components:
\begin{align*}
   \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -5 \end{pmatrix} - 4 \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix} &= \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -5 \end{pmatrix} + 4 \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -7 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -5 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ -28 \end{pmatrix} \\
   &= \begin{pmatrix} 2 + 4 \\ -5 + (-28) \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ -33 \end{pmatrix}
\end{align*}
So, the result is $\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ -33 \end{pmatrix}}$.

The expression $77\cdot 88\cdot 99$ can be simplified using modulo arithmetic. We will simplify each number modulo 20:

   \begin{align*}
   77 &\equiv 17 \pmod{20}\\
   88 &\equiv 8 \pmod{20}\\
   99 &\equiv 19 \pmod{20}
   \end{align*}

Now, we will find the product modulo 20:

   \begin{align*}
   (77\cdot 88\cdot 99) &\equiv (17 \cdot 8 \cdot 19) \pmod{20}\\
   &\equiv (17 \cdot (8 \cdot 19)) \pmod{20}\\
   &\equiv (17 \cdot (152)) \pmod{20}\\
   &\equiv (17 \cdot 12) \pmod{20}\\
   &\equiv 204 \pmod{20}\\
   &\equiv 4 \pmod{20}\\
   &\equiv n \pmod{20}
   \end{align*}

Thus, $n = \boxed{4}$

