solution:
The key here is to use the difference of squares identity twice.
\begin{align*}
1003^2 - 997^2 - 1001^2 + 999^2
& = (1003 + 997)(1003 - 997) - (1001 + 999)(1001 - 999)\\
& = 2000(6) - 2000(2) \\
& = \boxed{8000}
\end{align*}

To find all possible values for $x$ that allow the triangle to exist, we must apply the Triangle Inequality Theorem. This theorem states that the sum of the lengths of any two sides of a triangle must be greater than the length of the remaining side.

Let's write down all three inequalities:
\[ x^2 + 7 > 10 \Rightarrow x^2 > 3 \]
\[ x^2 + 10 > 7 \Rightarrow x^2 > -3 \]
\[ 10 + 7 > x^2 \Rightarrow x^2 < 17 \]

The inequality $x^2 > -3$ is always true for any positive value of $x$. The other two inequalities give us constraints on $x$:
   \begin{align*}
   x^2 > 3 &\Rightarrow x > \sqrt{3} \\
   x^2 < 17 &\Rightarrow x < \sqrt{17}
   \end{align*}

This means that for a triangle to exist, $x$ must satisfy both $x > \sqrt{3}$ and $x < \sqrt{17}$. The possible integer values of $x$ in this range are:
   \begin{align*}
   2, 3, 4
   \end{align*}

So, the answer is:
\[ \boxed{2, 3, 4} \]

